what makes someone a hero there is never  just  one answer to that question some will  tell you that it's selflessness  putting other people before oneself that  makes someone  heroic others believe that heroism takes  someone with a clear sense of morality  the ability to tell right from wrong  with absolute  certainty perhaps a hero should also be  a symbol  a paragon of hope and virtue for all of  society to look up to  and aspire to be and then there are  those who would argue that a person  can't possibly be a hero  unless they possess one key trait  whether that comes as a result of a  freak accident  gamma radiation exposure or mutated  genes  being blessed with extraordinary powers  and the will to use them for good  might just be what elevates a moral  selfless and  symbolic hero into something more a  super  hero it is rare that the scp foundation  encounters an anomalous creature or  entity that it considers to be harmless  there are of course exceptions but  perhaps even more of a rarity is an scp  that seeks to go out of its way and use  its anomalous abilities to do good  so many of the creatures and entities  kept contained by the foundation  have malicious intent like damage  regenerating reptiles with contempt for  humanity  and eldritch beings with desires to take  over this dimension  but then there is scp-2800 or as he  prefers to call himself  cactus man the spiked menace partially  human  and part succulent plant scp-2800 is one  of a rare breed of scps  one that aims to help people rather than  killing them  enslaving them or wiping reality as we  know it from existence  and as you might be surprised to learn  that this superhero known as cactus man  began life as one  daniel mcintyre an average guy from  scotland  little is known about daniel's origin  story all superheroes have one of course  but as far as foundation researchers are  aware  cactus man wasn't jettisoned in a pod  from his dying homeworld to the safety  of earth  it is also safe to assume he didn't get  pricked by a radioactive cactus  or have his dna infused with a plant  during a genetic experiment  he was first encountered by the scp  foundation whilst they were trying to  contain  another scp a reality warping object  that had somehow breached containment  what foundation staff tracking the  object witnessed was cactus man  attempting to assault the escaped scp  too little success following this  encounter  foundation personnel convinced cactus  man to allow them to contain him  he complied was designated as scp-2800  and researchers began investigating the  nature of this strange would-be  superhero according to daniel one day  his powers just  happened with little understanding as to  how why  or what had caused this transformation  when asked about how he acquired his  powers during an interview with scp  foundation researcher dr love  daniel said taviana stock i don't know  i woke up one day and boom cactus powers  thought i might as well use them for  good right  i always grew up reading a lot of comic  books always loved the x-men as a little  kid  so i thought i was one of them i thought  i was the luckiest guy in the world  ending up with super powers doesn't  every kid wish they could be a superhero  analysis by foundation research staff  revealed that daniel's dna had somehow  merged with the genome of a carnegie  gigantea plant or a saguaro cactus  this plant is usually what most people  picture if they were to imagine a  typical cactus  and is known to be native to the sonoran  desert as well as the mexican state of  sonora  how one became part of daniel mcintyre's  genetic makeup is baffling  it seems highly unlikely that a saguaro  cactus would grow naturally in scotland  given that the country has a far damper  and colder climate than the scorching  hot deserts that saguaros normally  thrive in  regardless of exactly how daniel became  fused with a cactus  his body shares a number of the same  physical properties of the plant  pointed spikes protrude from his skin  which can grow to just over an inch in  length  it seems that scp-2800 can either remove  these spikes manually with little pain  or will eventually shed them naturally  over time allowing more to regrow in  their place  as well as outwardly looking like an  anthropomorphic cactus  scp-2800 also shares various biological  traits with his cacti counterparts  daniel's body no longer functions in the  same way as that of an ordinary human  being in a number of different ways  firstly he is able to perform  photosynthesis deriving the necessary  nutrients he requires from direct  sunlight  this negates the need for him to consume  any food  and prevents him from feeling hunger or  the fatigue this can often bring  additionally his altered biology allows  cactus men to store more water than  would normally be possible for the  average human  and he requires less of it too scp-2800  is able to keep himself hydrated with a  third of the required fluids for an  average person daniel can also adapt to  more arid environments  with drier climates and above average  levels of heat having little  impact on his abilities speaking of  abilities  scp-2800 is not just a man with the  physical and biological traits of a  saguaro cactus  he also has superpowers that seem well  let's say  inspired by a cactus while perhaps not  as flashy as being faster than a  speeding bullet  more powerful than a locomotive or able  to leap tall buildings in a single bound  cactus man does possess his own unique  set of superhuman  abilities derived like his other traits  from his parts saguaro dna  scp-2800 has the power to empathetically  communicate with other plant life  unlike telepathy and the ability to  communicate solely through thoughts  empaths like cactus men are able to  influence or interpret the emotions or  moods of others so similar but a little  more subtle  in its effectiveness cactus man might  have superhuman powers alter dna and a  mysterious origin  but another part of a hero's journey is  the struggle and scp-2800  is no exception to this either despite  his desire to do good  he harbors a lot of unrest under that  prickly exterior  after extensive psychological  examination by the researchers at the  scp foundation  daniel was diagnosed with two distinct  mental disorders  the first of these is dysmithia or  chronic depression  with the other being a condition  colloquially known as hero syndrome  hero syndrome as its name suggests is  often characterized by an  unstoppable pathological urge to help  people  usually ignoring any risks to oneself in  the pursuit of assisting even total  strangers  some with this disorder will even  attempt to manufacture dangerous  scenarios in order to act like the hero  and earn themselves recognition and  praise for reacting heroically to the  danger they  secretly caused like for example  committing arson so they can save people  from a burning building  scp-2800 has never attempted anything  like this so far  but cactus man does express an extreme  willingness to help people  and try to intervene in any situation  that he thinks he can assist with  the problem is scp-2800 is hardly an  experienced crime fighter  and this has put him on the receiving  end of his fair share of  injuries during his first outing as  cactus man the spiked menace  daniel encountered a group engaging in  the sale of illicit substances  and attempted to apprehend them while he  was able to deal a cactus spine-filled  blow to one of their faces  the group quickly overpowered cactus men  and beat him until local law enforcement  arrived to save him  determined to prove himself a hero  though daniel returned to patrolling the  streets soon after  but met with the same results even weak  petty criminals seemed like they were  too much for cactus man to handle  while his hero syndrome compels scp-2800  to want to do good and  set a good example it is also directly  linked to his other condition  his dysmithia by attempting and failing  to be heroic  cactus man becomes chronically depressed  yet still has the urges brought on by  his hero syndrome to put himself in  harm's way for the sake of others  and when he is unable to provide help  daniel falls back into depression  it's a very difficult cycle in the hopes  of counteracting some of daniel's  struggles  the scp foundation have gifted him a  pair of potted cacti  these occupy scp-2800 cell with him  both oxygenating his room as well as  boosting his morale  although he has remarked that the cacti  don't say much to him beyond i'm thirsty  and  i am a cactus daniel has affectionately  named his potted plants they're now  known as cactilad  and spiky girl his sidekicks in the  never ending battle against evil  during interviews with foundation  researcher dr love  daniel admitted that he was a victim of  bullying throughout much of his  childhood  from a young age he often found himself  in physical altercations with bullies  that singled him out and picked on him  at school  cactus man said that his experiences  encouraged him to give back  and that despite having suffered at the  hands of bullies it made scp-2800  determined to help others  in need in his own words daniel didn't  want what happened to him  to happen to anybody else and it is  highly likely that these experiences  from his youth are at least part of the  cause of his hero syndrome  however another incident may also be  linked to scp-2800's condition  despite not often prevailing against  petty criminals there is cctv  surveillance footage of cactus man from  before his containment by the scp  foundation  the footage in question was taken at a  subway close to where daniel patrolled  and looked for criminals to apprehend  in the surveillance tape a woman and her  child can be seen waiting at the subway  station near a support pillar  from behind the pillar an assailant in a  mask appeared wielding what looked to be  a knife  the woman cowering and trying to protect  her child was made to open her purse  as the attacker threatened her with his  knife but then  cactus man appeared behind the man he  walked up to him  and punched him in his lower back and  chest a number of scp-2800  sharp cacti spines ended up lodged in  the man's skin  causing him to drop the knife in pain  during the ensuing scuffle  scp-2800 was able to tie the man up  thus saving the woman and her child the  woman then thanked cactus man  shaking his hand and embracing him her  child also expressed gratitude  with scp-2800 kneeling down to face them  and appearing to get emotional  at receiving recognition after signing  an autograph for the child  cactus man then disappeared from the  scene before police arrived  cacti have the tenacity to grow in  barren desert environments  surviving on very little water it is for  that reason  that to some these plants have come to  symbolize strength  resilience and endurance this one  encounter captured in this surveillance  footage may well have been one of the  few times cactus man  ever succeeded at being heroic but  perhaps it is all he needed to encourage  him to keep trying  to seek out wrongdoings time and time  again  even if it led to him being injured  maybe knowing that just once he had  succeeded in saving a woman  and her child was enough to convince him  that he would one day be able to do so  again and maybe that is what makes  someone  a true hero the power to endure  now check out scp-682 waze scp  foundation tried to kill hard to destroy  reptile  and scp-096 the shy guy for more  anomalies that have the power to endure  in spades
 

